cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "Please cite this repository when using its independently obtained finite witness or verification materials."
title: "An Independent Counterexample to WOWII Conjecture 291"
type: dataset
authors:
  - family-names: "Teagualicious"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Teagualicious/WOWII-Conjecture-291"
url: "https://github.com/Teagualicious/WOWII-Conjecture-291"
license: MIT
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: 2026-07-23
keywords:
  - graph theory
  - total domination
  - Havel-Hakimi
  - counterexample
  - Written on the Wall II
abstract: >-
  An alternative, independently obtained 12-vertex, 25-edge finite witness
  refuting WOWII Conjecture 291, with machine-readable graph data and a
  dependency-free verification script. This repository makes no claim of first
  discovery or publication priority. An earlier public 12-vertex, 21-edge
  counterexample and infinite family were posted in google-deepmind/formal-conjectures
  issue #4562.
references:
  - type: generic
    title: "Counterexample to Written on the Wall II Conjecture 291"
    authors:
      - family-names: "vulnix0x4"
    url: "https://github.com/google-deepmind/formal-conjectures/issues/4562"
    notes: "Earlier public counterexample and infinite family; the smallest member has 12 vertices and 21 edges."
